  "problem": {
    "id": "train-6185",
    "question": "A factory produces 90 refrigerators per hour. It also produces 70 more coolers than refrigerators per hour. How many products did the factory produce for 5 days if it works 9 hours a day?",
    "gold": "11250",
    "answer": "The factory produces 90 + 70 = <<90+70=160>>160 coolers per hour.\nThe factory works 5 * 9 = <<5*9=45>>45 hours in 5 days.\nThe factory produces ( 90 + 160) * 45 = <<(90+160)*45=11250>>11250 products for 5 days.\n#### 11250"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine the total number of products produced by the factory in 5 days, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the number of coolers produced per hour.\n2. Calculate the total number of refrigerators produced in one day.\n3. Calculate the total number of coolers produced in one day.\n4. Calculate the total number of products produced in one day.\n5. Calculate the total number of products produced in 5 days.\n\nLet's start with the first step:\n\n1. The factory produces 90 refrigerators per hour. It also produces 70 more coolers than refrigerators per hour. Therefore, the number of coolers produced per hour is:\n   \\[\n   90 + 70 = 160\n   \\]\n\n2. The factory works 9 hours a day. So, the total number of refrigerators produced in one day is:\n   \\[\n   90 \\times 9 = 810\n   \\]\n   And the total number of coolers produced in one day is:\n   \\[\n   160 \\times 9 = 1440\n   \\]\n\n3. The total number of products produced in one day is the sum of the refrigerators and coolers produced:\n   \\[\n   810 + 1440 = 2250\n   \\]\n\n4. The factory works for 5 days. So, the total number of products produced in 5 days is:\n   \\[\n   2250 \\times 5 = 11250\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of products produced by the factory in 5 days is \\(\\boxed{11250}\\).",
